{
  "mark.3.p1.b1": {
    "text": "Once again Jesus entered the synagogue,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:1"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p1.b2": {
    "text": "And a man with a withered hand was there.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:1"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p1.b3": {
    "text": "They were watching to see if He would heal on the Sabbath.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:2"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p1.b4": {
    "text": "In order to accuse Jesus,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:2"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p2.b1": {
    "text": "Then Jesus said to the man with the withered hand,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:3"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p2.b2": {
    "text": "Stand up among us.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:3"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p2.b3": {
    "text": "And He asked them,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:4"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p2.b4": {
    "text": "Which is lawful on the Sabbath: to do good or to do evil,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:4"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p2.b5": {
    "text": "To save life or to destroy it?",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:4"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p2.b6": {
    "text": "But they were silent.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:4"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p3.b1": {
    "text": "Jesus looked around at them with anger",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:5"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p3.b2": {
    "text": "And sorrow at their hardness of heart.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:5"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p3.b3": {
    "text": "Then He said to the man,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:5"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p3.b4": {
    "text": "Stretch out your hand.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:5"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p3.b5": {
    "text": "So he stretched it out,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:5"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p3.b6": {
    "text": "And it was restored.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:5"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p4.b1": {
    "text": "At this, the Pharisees went out",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:6"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p4.b2": {
    "text": "And began plotting with the Herodians",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:6"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p4.b3": {
    "text": "How they might kill Jesus.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:6"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p5.b1": {
    "text": "So Jesus withdrew with His disciples to the sea, accompanied by a large crowd from Galilee,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:7"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p5.b2": {
    "text": "Judea, Jerusalem, Idumea,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:7-8"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p5.b3": {
    "text": "The region beyond the Jordan, and the vicinity of Tyre and Sidon.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:8"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p5.b4": {
    "text": "The large crowd came to Him when they heard what great things He was doing.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:8"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p6.b1": {
    "text": "Jesus asked His disciples to have a boat ready for Him so that the crowd would not crush Him.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:9"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p6.b2": {
    "text": "For He had healed so many that all who had diseases were pressing forward to touch Him.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:10"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p7.b1": {
    "text": "And when the unclean spirits saw Him, they fell down before Him",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:11"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p7.b2": {
    "text": "And cried out,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:11"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p7.b3": {
    "text": "You are the Son of God!",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:11"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p7.b4": {
    "text": "But He warned them sternly not to make Him known.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:12"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p8.b1": {
    "text": "Then Jesus went up on the mountain",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:13"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p8.b2": {
    "text": "And called for those He wanted,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:13"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p8.b3": {
    "text": "And they came to Him.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:13"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p9.b1": {
    "text": "He appointed twelve of them, whom He designated as apostles,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:14"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p9.b2": {
    "text": "To accompany Him,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:14"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p9.b3": {
    "text": "To be sent out to preach,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:14"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p9.b4": {
    "text": "And to have authority to drive out demons.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:15"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p10.b1": {
    "text": "These are the twelve He appointed: Simon (whom He named Peter),",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:16"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p10.b2": {
    "text": "James son of Zebedee and his brother John",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:17"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p10.b3": {
    "text": "(whom He named Boanerges, meaning “Sons of Thunder”),",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:17"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p11.b1": {
    "text": "Andrew,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:18"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p11.b2": {
    "text": "Philip, Bartholomew,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:18"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p11.b3": {
    "text": "Matthew,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:18"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p11.b4": {
    "text": "Thomas, James son of Alphaeus,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:18"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p11.b5": {
    "text": "Thaddaeus, Simon the Zealot,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:18"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p11.b6": {
    "text": "And Judas Iscariot, who betrayed Jesus.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:19"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p12.b1": {
    "text": "Then Jesus went home, and once again a crowd gathered,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:20"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p12.b2": {
    "text": "So that He and His disciples could not even eat.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:20"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p12.b3": {
    "text": "When His family heard about this, they went out to take custody of Him,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:21"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p12.b4": {
    "text": "Saying, “He is out of His mind.”",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:21"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p13.b1": {
    "text": "And the scribes who had come down from Jerusalem were saying,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:22"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p13.b2": {
    "text": "He is possessed by Beelzebul,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:22"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p13.b3": {
    "text": "And,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:22"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p13.b4": {
    "text": "By the prince of the demons He drives out demons.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:22"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p14.b1": {
    "text": "So Jesus called them together and began to speak to them in parables:",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:23"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p14.b2": {
    "text": "How can Satan drive out Satan?",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:23"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p14.b3": {
    "text": "If a kingdom is divided against itself, it cannot stand.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:24"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p14.b4": {
    "text": "If a house is divided against itself, it cannot stand.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:25"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p15.b1": {
    "text": "And if Satan is divided and rises against himself, he cannot stand;",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:26"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p15.b2": {
    "text": "His end has come.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:26"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p15.b3": {
    "text": "Indeed, no one can enter a strong man’s house to steal his possessions",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:27"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p15.b4": {
    "text": "Unless he first ties up the strong man.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:27"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p15.b5": {
    "text": "Then he can plunder his house.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:27"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p16.b1": {
    "text": "Truly I tell you, the sons of men will be forgiven all sins and blasphemies, as many as they utter.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:28"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p16.b2": {
    "text": "But whoever blasphemes against the Holy Spirit will never be forgiven;",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:29"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p16.b3": {
    "text": "He is guilty of eternal sin.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:29"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p16.b4": {
    "text": "Jesus made this statement because they were saying,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:30"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p16.b5": {
    "text": "He has an unclean spirit.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:30"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p17.b1": {
    "text": "Then Jesus’ mother and brothers came and stood outside.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:31"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p17.b2": {
    "text": "They sent someone in to summon Him,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:31"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p17.b3": {
    "text": "And a crowd was sitting around Him.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:32"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p17.b4": {
    "text": "He was told,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:32"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p17.b5": {
    "text": "Look, … Your mother and brothers are outside, asking for You.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:32"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p18.b1": {
    "text": "But Jesus replied,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:33"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p18.b2": {
    "text": "Who are My mother…",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:33"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p18.b3": {
    "text": "…and My brothers?",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:33"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p18.b4": {
    "text": "Looking at those seated in a circle around Him, He said,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:34"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p18.b5": {
    "text": "Here are My mother and My brothers!",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:34"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p18.b6": {
    "text": "For whoever does the will of God",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:35"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.3.p18.b7": {
    "text": "Is My brother and sister and mother.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 3:35"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  }
}
